Why is Media considered an abstract class?

Because it contains virtual functions.


What is the purpose of a pure virtual function?

To enable a function to be called by its derivative classes without maintaining a definition of its own.

What does the * mean in Media* library[5]?

It indicates that the library is a collection of Media pointers

Why can a pointer of type Media* refer to an object of type Song?

Song is a derivitive of type Media and thus can be referred this way

Why should objects created using new be released using delete?

Because they will not delete themselves and are not always going to be garbage collected. 
